######
#
# HX-2018-03-11:
# The release process of ATS-Postiats(ATS2).
#
# HX-2026-10-21:
# ATS1 is NOT needed anymore: the compiler (src/) is written in ATS2 and
# compiles itself (see src/README and src/PORTING.md).
#
######
#
# The script for building a release:
# ${PATSHOME}/share/SCRIPT/build_release.sh
#
######
#
# First,
# update $PATSHOME/VERSION
# which affects the following:
# $PATSHOME/doc/DISTRIB/ATS-Postiats/configure.ac
# $PATSHOME/src/pats_basics.sats (PATS_{MAJOR,MINOR,MICRO}_VERSION)
# $PATSHOME/CHANGES-ats2 (a section that bears the version)
#
# The script share/SCRIPT/check_release_version.sh checks that all of
# them declare the same version:
#
# sh ${PATSHOME}/share/SCRIPT/check_release_version.sh
#
#
# If using Nix, run `nix-shell nix/shell.nix` from $PATSHOME.
#
# Second,
# execute the following command-line from doc/DISTRIB:
#
# make -f Makefile.gen
#
# to generate Makefile based on Makefile.atxt
#
######
#
# Packaging ATS
#
# Note that x.y.z is the version
# you want to build in the following command:
#
# cd /tmp
# sh ${PATSHOME}/share/SCRIPT/build_release.sh x.y.z KIND
# <
# KIND is 'intknd', 'gmpknd', 'both' or 'contrib'. The tarball
# ATS2-Postiats-x.y.z.tgz is one for both kinds of integers of the
# constraint solver: ./configure uses libgmp when <gmp.h> is there.
#
# The built packages:
# /tmp/ATS-Postiats/doc/DISTRIB/ATS2-Postiats-x.y.z.tgz
# /tmp/ATS-Postiats/doc/DISTRIB/ATS2-Postiats-contrib-x.y.z.tgz
# /tmp/ATS-Postiats/doc/DISTRIB/ATS2-Postiats-include-x.y.z.tgz
#
# From a clone that is already built, `make dist` (the root Makefile; see
# INSTALL) makes ATS2-Postiats-x.y.z.tgz and ATS2-Postiats-include-x.y.z.tgz
# with their .sha256 files.
# >
# rm -rf /tmp/ATS-Postiats
# rm -rf /tmp/ATS-Postiats-contrib
#
# The packages can also be built by hand:
#
# cd ${PATSHOME}
# make -f Makefile_devl bin_atsdoc  # atsdoc generates the packaging scripts
# make -C src CBOOT                  # (only to refresh the tracked bootstrap bundle)
# cd doc/DISTRIB
# make -f Makefile.gen
# make atspackaging                 # fills in ATS-Postiats/
# make atspacktarzvcf            # ATS2-Postiats-x.y.z.tgz
# make -f Makefile_inclats tarzvcf  # ATS2-Postiats-include-x.y.z.tgz
#
#######
#
# Releasing ATS
#
# The release notes of a version are generated from the changelog:
#
# sh ${PATSHOME}/share/SCRIPT/make_release_notes.sh x.y.z
#
# which writes
# ${PATSHOME}/doc/DISTRIB/ATS-Postiats/RELEASE/ats2-postiats-x.y.z-release.html
#
# Create a GitHub Release of the tag vx.y.z (github.com/msorc/ATS-Postiats)
# and upload the following files to it, with their .sha256 files
# (`make dist` writes them):
#
# ATS2-Postiats-x.y.z.tgz
# ATS2-Postiats-contrib-x.y.z.tgz
# ATS2-Postiats-include-x.y.z.tgz
# ats2-postiats-x.y.z-release.html
#
# The changes for the above release.html file can be found in
# ${PATSHOME}/CHANGES-ats2.
#
#######

###### end of [README] ######
